1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,780
Welcome back. Today our guest is an atom, and
the question is personal: why do you absorb
X-rays?

2
00:00:07,780 --> 00:00:14,648
The atom says: I only take energy packets that
can kick an inner electron into an allowed
state.

3
00:00:14,648 --> 00:00:21,036
Below the edge, the photon is too weak. It
knocks, but nobody answers.

4
00:00:21,036 --> 00:00:28,504
At the edge, the photon has enough energy to
launch a core electron. The absorption jumps.

5
00:00:28,504 --> 00:00:36,428
Near the edge, the outgoing electron wave feels
the local chemistry and shape of empty states.

6
00:00:36,428 --> 00:00:45,360
That is why XAS can tell oxidation state,
coordination, and local structure without asking
the crystal to behave.
